	"roles": {
		"waterseller": {"title": "Water-seller", "work": "plaza",
			"intro": ["Water! Sweet water, cool from the deep well! For you, Captain, only twice the price.", "{name}. I sell the one thing nobody here can do without. Business is good. Business is always good."],
			"self": ["My well is the deepest on the island. Forty fathoms of rope, and I've climbed every one of them twice.",
				"Gold, they say, is worth its weight in gold. Out on the dunes, water's worth more, and it weighs a great deal less."],
				"talk": ["Twelve buckets before sunrise, and that's on a lazy day. The rope has worn my hands to leather.",
					"People haggle over water. Then they get thirsty and stop haggling. I'm a patient man.",
					"A sandstorm is bad for everyone but me. After one, the whole town queues at my well.",
					"My worry? The well running dry. I lower the bucket each dawn and listen hard for the splash.",
					"I once sold a cup to a camel. He paid with a kick. Fair price, I suppose.",
					"Rain fell here when I was nine. I stood in it and cried. Terrible for business, rain."]},
		"guide": {"title": "Caravan guide", "work": "forage",
			"intro": ["You want to cross the sand? Don't. You want to anyway? Then you want me.", "{name}. I read the dunes. They move, you know. Every night. Just enough to lose you."],
			"self": ["I've walked to the far side and back eleven times. The twelfth time is the one that kills a guide, so I'm in no hurry.",
				"Follow the rocks, never the sand. Rocks stay where they're put. Sand has its own ideas."],
				"talk": ["Today I took three merchants to the oasis and brought back three merchants. A good day.",
					"The dunes sing before a storm. Most hear wind. I hear 'turn around, fool.'",
					"Camels are smarter than people. They just don't want you to know it.",
					"What keeps me up at night? Raiders on the eastern track. They wait where the rocks pinch together.",
					"I plant a red rag on a pole at every camp. When the poles vanish, I know the dunes walked.",
					"A client asked me if we were lost. I said no. We were, for two days. He never knew."]},
		"potter": {"title": "Potter", "work": "market",
			"intro": ["Mind the jars! Every one of them holds water or wine or my temper.", "{name}. Potter. The clay's from the wadi bed. The cracks are from the sun."],
			"self": ["I glazed the blue dome on the palace when I was a girl. Climbed up with a bucket and came down with a reputation.",
				"A good jar keeps water cool all day. A bad one keeps it for an hour, then gives it to the sand."],
				"talk": ["Fired the kiln this morning. Twenty jars went in, eighteen came out. The sun took two.",
					"The wadi clay's getting thin. One more dry year and I'll be making cups out of hope.",
					"Every jar I make has a thumbprint inside the lip. My signature. Nobody ever looks.",
					"A sailor broke three of my jars yesterday. He's paying for them in labour. Look, there he is.",
					"Clay remembers every mistake. So do I. Clay is kinder about it.",
					"I dream of making a jar big enough to hold the whole sea. Then I'd sell it back to the fish."]},
		"spicer": {"title": "Spice merchant", "work": "market",
			"intro": ["Saffron, cumin, pepper from three seas! Smell that. That's the smell of money leaving your purse.", "{name}. I deal in spice. And gossip. The gossip's free, mostly."],
			"self": ["My grandfather crossed the sand sea with forty camels and one sack of pepper. He came back with one camel and forty sacks.",
				"Everyone thinks the spice comes from here. None of it does. Don't tell anyone."],
				"talk": ["A sack of saffron came in wet this morning. Do you know what wet saffron smells like? Tears.",
					"My nose is my fortune. I asked the council to insure it. They laughed. I still asked.",
					"I sneezed in the pepper once. Lost a month's profit on the wind. Never again.",
					"The raiders took a caravan of cloves last moon. Now their whole camp smells like a feast day.",
					"Cinnamon for love, cumin for luck, pepper for revenge. Ask my old partner.",
					"Trade's slow when the sea's rough. The spice keeps. My patience doesn't."]},
		"storyteller": {"title": "Storyteller", "work": "plaza",
			"intro": ["Sit in the shade, Captain. I'll tell you of the city under the sand. Every word true, or close.", "Old {name}. I keep the tales. The wind keeps trying to blow them away."],
			"self": ["I've told of the buried city so often I can walk its streets in my sleep. I don't, though. Some of them aren't empty.",
				"When I was young the thing under the dunes was a tale for children. Now the children won't go past the last palm."],
				"talk": ["My throat is dry from telling the tale of the sand king three times today. They want it again.",
					"A good story needs a monster. Lately the desert has been very generous with those.",
					"I add a little to every tale each time I tell it. In thirty years the sand king has grown nine feet.",
					"The young ones laugh at the old tales now. Then the wind howls, and they sit a little closer.",
					"Someday someone will tell a tale about you, Captain. Make it a good one. I hate sad endings.",
					"I lost my voice once for a week. The town was so quiet they thought I'd died."]},
		"watcher": {"title": "Lookout", "work": "nets",
			"intro": ["Saw your sails through the haze at noon. Thought you were a mirage. You still might be.", "{name}. I watch the sea and the sand. Trouble comes from both."],
			"self": ["The haze lies. A ship looks close when it's far and far when it's on top of you. I've learned to count, not look.",
				"I can tell a sandstorm coming by the colour of the gulls. Don't ask me how. They go grey."],
				"talk": ["Three sails this morning. Two were fishing boats. One was a cloud. I counted it anyway.",
					"Sitting up here all day, you start talking to the gulls. They're poor listeners.",
					"I worry about the haze. A raider ship could sit just inside it, and I'd never see her.",
					"My eyes are better than any spyglass. My back, though, is worse than any old mast.",
					"I ring the bell twice for ships, three times for storms, and once when I want my lunch brought up.",
					"When the dust rises inland, I watch the sand as hard as the sea. Something walks out there."]},
		"healer": {"title": "Healer", "work": "home",
			"intro": ["Sit down before you fall down. Sun-sick, all of you foreigners.", "I'm {name}. Aloe for burns, salt for wounds, shade for fools."],
			"self": ["Half the sickness here is the sun and the other half is people who won't stay out of it.",
				"Scorpion stings I can treat. Scorpion stings from the big ones out on the flats, I can only pray over."],
				"talk": ["Six sunburns and a scorpion sting before noon. Nobody listens to me about hats.",
					"I grow aloe on my roof. The goats keep trying to eat it. The goats and I are at war.",
					"The worst patient is a proud man. The second worst is a proud man with heatstroke.",
					"My supplies run low every summer. Bandages, honey, salt. I pray for the trade ships.",
					"A boy swallowed a date stone yesterday. He's fine. The date stone lives in a jar now.",
					"I've stitched up three of the lookout's fingers this year. He keeps grabbing hot rope."]},
	},
	"barks": {
		"day": ["Hot enough to bake bread on the walls. My wife does, some days.", "Keep your head covered, stranger. The sun here bites.", "The wind's turning. Close your shutters by evening.",
			"Not a cloud. Never a cloud. I'd trade a camel for one cloud.", "Drink before you're thirsty. By the time you're thirsty it's late.", "Everything here is sand, eventually. Even us.",
			"The well bucket came up warm today. Warm! From the bottom of the earth.", "Noon soon. Everybody inside till the shadows stretch.",
			"My sandals are melting. Look. Look at that.", "A caravan's due from the dunes. Pray they found the wells.", "The goats won't leave the shade. Smart goats.",
			"Even the lizards are hiding. You should be too.", "Water first, talk after. That's manners here.", "The souk smells of cumin and sweat. Lovely.",
			"Listen. Dry wind off the flats, dry as old bone.", "Sun on the dome so bright you could go blind looking.", "A sailor fainted on the quay this morning. Hats, people. Hats.",
			"If you see shade, take it. Someone else will if you don't.", "Spice on the air and sand in my teeth. Another day.", "The dates are ripening fast in this heat."],
		"evening": ["Finally. The sand's cooling. The town wakes up now.", "Light the lamps. The souk opens properly after dark.", "Sunset over the dunes. Never gets old. I'm getting old.",
			"Hear that? Wind over the crests. Sounds like singing, if you've been out long enough.", "The heat's breaking. I can feel my brain again.",
			"Smell that? Lamb on the coals at the caravanserai.", "Evening prayers soon. Then the music.", "Look at the sky go red. Sandstorm tomorrow, or a good omen.",
			"The dunes turn purple now. Purple! Like spilled wine.", "Time to water the palms, before the cold steals it.", "Children out at last. They've been caged in shade all day.",
			"The caravan came in at dusk. Camels and gossip both.", "Let the shutters open. Let the breeze in.", "Last call at the water stalls. Then it's tea or nothing.",
			"The fishermen bring the boats in red as the sky.", "Music from the square tonight. Drums, if the drummer's sober.", "My bones like this hour. Not too hot, not too cold.",
			"Stars coming out over the sand. One, two... too many.", "Shadows long as masts. Walk in them while you can."],
		"night": ["Cold, now. Who'd believe the same sky could be so cruel both ways?", "Stay in the town after dark. Things come up out of the sand at night.",
			"So many stars. My grandmother said each one's a lost caravan's fire.", "Wrap up. The sand gives back its heat by midnight.",
			"Hear the clicking? Scorpions hunting. Stay on the stones.", "The well's locked at night. Thieves, and worse.", "Lamps in every window. The dark out here is very big.",
			"Can't sleep. Too cold to sleep, too tired to stay up.", "Something howled out on the flats. Not a jackal.", "Moon on the dunes. Pretty as silver, and just as cold.",
			"Shh. Listen. The sand's shifting out there.", "My grandfather crossed the dunes at night, by the stars. Once.", "The caravanserai's still lit. Someone's losing money at dice.",
			"Night watch again. The night watch is always me.", "Bandits ride on dark nights. Keep your purse close.", "Blanket, tea, a fire. That's all a man needs out here.",
			"Even the sea goes quiet at night here. Listening, maybe.", "Shooting star! Make a wish. Wish for rain.", "Fire's low. Throw on another dung cake, would you?"],
		"nets": ["The fish come in close when the sand blows. Something about the shade.", "Hold that end. Tighter. No, tighter.", "Salt in the nets, salt on the quay, salt in my bread.",
			"Mend the tear before the sun dries the knots.", "Sand crabs in the net again. Bad eating and worse company.", "A good net lasts five years here. This one's on its ninth.",
			"The tide brings fish and the wind brings sand. Guess which fills the nets."],
		"forage": ["Scorpion tracks. Fresh. Watch your boots.", "Dates here, if the birds left any.", "See that shimmer? Water, or the sun lying again.",
			"Wild thyme in the rocks. Smells like home.", "Careful. That rock's been in the sun since dawn.", "Snake skin. Big one. Moving on, quickly.",
			"Found an old coin in the sand. The desert gives, sometimes."],
		"dock": ["Tide's out. Everything stinks when the tide's out.", "Mind the ropes. Mind the stones. They're hot.", "Your ship rides high. Come to buy, then, not to sell?",
			"Unload the water casks first. Always the water first.", "Another ship from the north. Pale sailors, burning already.", "The planks warp in the sun. Step where the nails are.",
			"Gulls fight over fish guts here. Mind your hat."],
		"boats": ["These hulls are older than the town. The sea's kinder to wood than the sun is.", "Pitch, pitch and more pitch. The sun opens every seam.",
			"Turn her over, scrape her clean. Barnacles grow fast in warm water.", "That sail's patched with an old tent. Works better than new.", "Bring me rope, not advice.",
			"She leaks. They all leak. The trick is leaking slower than you bail.", "Painted her eyes fresh. A boat needs to see where she's going."],
		"stall": ["Fresh water, fresh fish, fresh lies. Pick two.", "Dates, figs, salt. Everything a sailor needs and nothing he wants.",
			"Two coins for the figs. Three if you keep staring at them like that.", "Taste first. Then pay. Then don't tell my wife I let you taste.",
			"Salted fish, sun-dried, straight off the racks.", "Shade's free. Sitting in it costs a date.", "Last waterskins before the caravan buys them all."],
		"market": ["Silk from the east! Well. From a ship that came from the east. Probably.", "Prices go up when the wind blows. The wind is blowing.", "Haggle, Captain. It's rude not to.",
			"Brass lamps! Rub one. No genie. Worth a try, though.", "Rugs from the inland looms, every knot tied by hand!",
			"Pickpockets love a crowd. Keep a hand on your coin, Captain.", "Spice from beyond the sand sea! Sneeze at your own risk."],
		"home": ["Sand in the bread again. Sand in everything.", "The children are on the roof. They're always on the roof.", "If you see a goat with a blue rope, it's mine.",
			"Sweep the step, and the wind fills it again. Every day.", "The water jar's half full. Or half empty. Either way, thirsty.",
			"Who left the door open? Now the house is full of dune.", "Bread's rising in the sun. Don't touch it."],
		"plaza": ["The fountain's running! Doesn't always. Drink while it does.", "Sit in the shade, all of you. The square's no place at noon.", "The council's arguing again. Hear them from here.",
			"Pigeons on the fountain again. Shoo! Drink somewhere else!", "The storyteller's on his stool. Pull up some shade.",
			"Coins in the fountain bring rain, they say. Never has yet.", "These tiles are hot enough to dance on. Some do."],
		"inn": ["Mint tea or something stronger? The something stronger's mint tea with rum.", "Caravans come, caravans go. The innkeeper stays rich.", "To the captains! May the wind be at their backs and not in their eyes.",
			"Camels in the yard, carpets on the floor. Welcome to the caravanserai.", "Best beds in the house are on the roof, under the stars.",
			"A merchant's paying for everyone's tea. Drink fast before he sobers up.", "Traveller's stew again. Nobody knows what's in it. Nobody asks."],
		"workshop": ["Hand me the tongs. No, the other tongs.", "Brass doesn't care how hot it is. I do.", "This lantern's for the caravan guide. Third one this year.",
			"Hammer, file, polish. The sand undoes all three by evening.", "Mind the kiln. It's hotter than the noon sun, and it never sets.",
			"Weaving's slow. A carpet is a year of someone's life underfoot.", "Leather for waterskins. Stitch it tight or carry an empty one."],
		"field": ["Climb up, cut the bunch, don't drop it. Simple. Mostly.", "The date palms want water and shade. So do I.", "Laundry dries in a breath out here. Then the wind takes it.",
			"Shake the sand out of the sheets before you fold them!", "Pollinate by hand, every palm. The bees won't come this far.",
			"Channel's dry again. Who opened the sluice to the far grove?", "Ripe dates, gold as coins. Sweeter, too."],
		"shrine": ["Light a lamp for those lost on the sand.", "Leave a cup of water here. The spirits get thirsty too.", "Quiet here. Even the wind keeps its voice down.",
			"I pray for rain. Every day. The answer's always the same.", "My father's name is carved on that stone. Lost with a caravan.",
			"Keep your shoes off the tiles. The old ones are watching.", "Beads of blue glass for luck. Take one. Sailors need it most."],
		"well": ["Lower the bucket slow. Bang the sides and the water clouds.", "Wait your turn. The well serves everyone, but in order.",
			"Cool water. Taste it. That's forty fathoms of cool.", "The rope's fraying. Who's paying for a new one? Not me.",
			"Don't lean over! It's a long way down and nobody fishes you out.", "They found a drowned scorpion in the bucket. Still angry."],
		"bench": ["Did you hear about the spice merchant's nephew? Well. I can't say.", "Sit, sit. The shade's big enough for two old fools.",
			"I've been on this bench since dawn. Somebody has to watch the street.", "The baker's girl and the lookout's boy are courting. Everyone knows but them.",
			"Back in my day the dunes were smaller. And so were the scorpions.", "Pass me a date. I'm resting from resting.",
			"Watch that sailor. Third time round the square. Lost, or lying."],
		"storehouse": ["Grain on the left, salt on the right, rum behind the lock.", "Lift with your legs! Sacks don't care about your back.",
			"Count the water casks again. Twice. The council will.", "Mice got into the dates. Fat mice, happy mice.",
			"Stack it high, keep it dry. Sand gets in, the stores go bad.", "Caravan stores in, ship stores out. The door never shuts.",
			"Something's chewed through the sacks. Scorpions don't chew. Do they?"],
		"pointer": ["If it's work you're after, {who} {where} has been complaining all week.", "{who}'s got trouble. {who} always has trouble. This one sounded real.",
			"Go and see {who} {where}. Nobody listens to {who}, and look where that's got us.",
			"{who} {where} keeps looking at the sea like help might sail in. That's you, maybe.",
			"Ask {who}. {who} has a problem bigger than the heat. Try {where}.",
			"You've a sword. {who} {where} has a worry. Seems a good match.",
			"{who} was asking after a strong back and a sharp blade, {where}.",
			"If you want coin, {who} {where} has been offering it to anyone who'll listen.",
			"Somebody should help {who}. Somebody isn't me. Maybe somebody's you.",
			"{who} {where} hasn't slept in days. Something's wrong, and it isn't the heat.",
			"Word is {who} needs a captain's help. You'll find them {where}.",
			"Talk to {who}. Nobody else will since the business with the goats.",
			"{who} came back from the dunes white as salt. Ask why, {where}."],
